{{define "title"}}Refund and cancellation policy - View MPP{{end}}

{{define "main"}}
<main class="page page--text legal centered">
{{template "crumbs" .}}
  <header class="page__head">
    <h1>Refunds and cancellation</h1>
  </header>

  <h2>Who you pay</h2>
  <p>
    Pro is sold through Paddle.com, our online reseller and the merchant of record for all our
    orders. Paddle takes the payment, adds sales tax or VAT where it applies, sends the receipt and
    pays out any refund. The purchase itself is covered by Paddle's
    <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/buyer-terms" rel="noopener">Buyer Terms</a> and
    <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/refund-policy" rel="noopener">refund policy</a>; this page
    says what we add on top.
  </p>

  <h2>The free trial</h2>
  <p>
    The 7-day trial needs no card and charges nothing. When it ends without a plan chosen, the
    account goes back to the free plan by itself.
  </p>

  <h2>Cancelling</h2>
  <p>
    You can cancel at any time from the account page, under Manage subscription, or by writing to
    <a href="mailto:support@viewmpp.com">support@viewmpp.com</a>. The next charge does not happen,
    and Pro stays on until the end of the month or year you have already paid for. Deleting your
    account cancels its subscription first.
  </p>

  <h2>Refunds</h2>
  <p>
    Ask within 14 days of your first payment for a plan and you get the whole amount back, for any
    reason. Write to <a href="mailto:support@viewmpp.com">support@viewmpp.com</a> from the address
    on your account, or reply to the Paddle receipt. Pro ends once the refund goes through.
  </p>
  <p>
    After those 14 days, and for renewals, the rest of a paid period is not refunded, unless the law
    where you live gives you that right. Consumers in the EU and the UK, for example, have a 14-day
    right to withdraw from a purchase, and Paddle's refund policy sets out how it applies.
  </p>
  <p>
    Refunds are paid by Paddle to the card or account you paid with. Under Paddle's policy that
    happens within 14 days of the refund being approved.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about a payment, a cancellation or a refund:
    <a href="mailto:support@viewmpp.com">support@viewmpp.com</a>. The full
    <a href="/terms">terms of use</a> cover everything else.
  </p>
  <p class="legal__meta">Last updated: 16 November 2026</p>
</main>

{{template "sitefooter" .}}
